//@version=6
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  THE MATHEMATICAL INDICATOR  ·  2-CANDLE BIAS STRATEGY
//  Story → Zone → Strat  |  Pine Script® v6  |  Overlay  |  MIT License
//  https://github.com/roan-maverick/tradingview-mathematical-indicator
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  THE STRATEGY IN PLAIN WORDS
//  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//   1. STORY   Two candles pick the direction for the whole session: yesterday's daily candle and
//              the last 4H candle before the session. Both green = only BUY. Both red = only SELL.
//              They disagree = MIXED: the story decides (daily level, weekly staircase, daily candle).
//   2. ZONE    Floors and ceilings are marked on candle BODIES. A level only breaks when a candle of
//              its OWN timeframe closes through it. Wicks through it make it stronger.
//              No buys under a daily ceiling, no sells over a daily floor: come back tomorrow.
//              Trades only happen inside clean zones: areas price already crossed without stopping.
//              If the pre-session candle already ran in the bias direction, wait for a pullback.
//   3. STRAT   Inside the first hour of a session: price pauses (a range with at least two opposite
//              candles), one strong candle closes outside it (never bigger than half the range),
//              the next candle dips back (the "rubber band" wick), then a stop order at the breakout
//              candle's high (low for sells) fires the entry. Stop loss beyond the breakout candle.
//   4. EXIT    1:1 first. At 1R the stop moves to breakeven (part of the trade can be closed there),
//              the rest rides to the next level. If price runs too fast in a straight line, take it.
//
//  INTEGRITY
//  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//   • Everything runs on CLOSED candles. Higher-timeframe data uses the previous CLOSED candle
//     (expr[1] + lookahead_on): nothing repaints.
//   • Entries are simulated from OHLC: a stop order fills when a later candle trades through it.
//     When the rubber band wick and the break happen in the same candle, the dip is assumed first.
//   • The on-chart record is this chart's history, no fees or slippage.
//   • Built for 5 to 15 minute charts on futures, forex, gold, indices and crypto.
//
//  HOW TO INSTALL: in the Pine Editor press Ctrl+A (Cmd+A on Mac) and delete the default code
//  FIRST, then paste this whole file. A script can only hold one indicator() declaration.
//
//  For education and research. Not financial advice.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

indicator("The Mathematical Indicator · 2-Candle Bias", shorttitle = "MATH", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_bars_back = 150)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
